{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Africa GATES — "We are Africa" band (globe)
   Sits directly after the hero on the homepage. Light band, dashed
   background guides, centred globe, dashed annotation card at its right,
   and the stat card overlapping the sphere's lower edge.

   Requires (see docs/GLOBE-BAND.md):
     <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/globe-band.css">
     <script src="/assets/js/vendor/d3-7.9.0.min.js"></script>
     <script src="/assets/js/vendor/topojson-client-3.1.0.min.js"></script>
     <script src="/assets/js/globe-band.js" defer></script>
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="reg" id="agGlobeBand">
  <div class="reg__guides" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

  <div class="hw reg__in">
    <div class="reg__hd">
      <h2 class="reg__h">{{ globe_heading|default('We are Africa') }}</h2>
      <p class="reg__sub">One verified index for the continent — <span class="reg__sub-em">close to voters, close to the record.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="reg__body">
      <div class="reg__stage" id="agGlobeStage"
           {% if globe_cities is defined %}data-cities="{{ globe_cities|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"{% endif %}
           data-topojson="{{ globe_topojson|default('/assets/geo/countries-110m.json') }}">
        <canvas id="agGlobe"></canvas>
        <div class="reg__layer" id="agGlobeNodes"></div>

        <div class="ccard" id="agGlobeCard" role="dialog" aria-label="Country detail">
          <div class="ccard__hd">
            <div>
              <p class="ccard__nm" data-globe-name>—</p>
              <p class="ccard__rg" data-globe-cities>—</p>
            </div>
            <button class="ccard__x" type="button" data-globe-close aria-label="Close">✕</button>
          </div>
          <div class="ccard__rows">
            <div class="crow"><span>Ballots this cycle</span><b data-globe-ballots>—</b></div>
            <div class="crow"><span>Verification node</span><b data-globe-node>—</b></div>
            <div class="crow"><span>Median verification</span><b data-globe-verify>—</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="reg__note">{{ globe_note|default('Every ballot is confirmed at the verification node nearest the voter — median 1.3 seconds, before it reaches the Cultural Power Index.') }}</aside>
    </div>

    {#
      ── THE FOUR FIGURES, AND WHY THREE OF THEM ARE NOT LITERALS ──────────

      The handoff hard-codes `45% + 55%` and `4`. Both are RULES this platform
      reads from `RuleEngine`, per cycle — `community_pct`/`judge_pct` come from
      `weights()` and the criteria count from the active rubric. CLAUDE.md is
      explicit that the split "is set per cycle rather than fixed forever", and
      this repo has already shipped four published promises that outlived the
      rule they described, on pages that stated a weighting as a constant.

      So they are passed in, with the design's values as the fallback for a
      deployment that has not configured a rubric yet. `/integrity` resolves
      `community_pct` exactly this way — one resolver, not two.

      `0–1,000` stays a literal: the index range is structural, not a setting.
    #}
    <div class="reg__cols">
      <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">{{ nations_count|default(54) }}</div><div class="reg__l">Nations in scope</div></div>
      <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">0–1,000</div><div class="reg__l">CPI score scale</div></div>
      <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">{{ community_pct|default(45) }}<small>%</small> + {{ judge_pct|default(55) }}<small>%</small></div><div class="reg__l">Public votes + jury</div></div>
      <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">{{ jury_criteria|default(4) }}</div><div class="reg__l">Jury criteri{{ jury_criteria|default(4) == 1 ? 'on' : 'a' }}</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
